    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A single chunk of a snapshot being transferred to a lagging replica.</para>
<para>Snapshot data is compressed on the sender side (e.g. with ZSTD) and split into fixed-size pieces. Each piece carries a SHA-256 checksum of its own payload so the receiver can detect corruption independently of adjacent chunks, tolerating network interruption and partial retries. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
